From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:21:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Give the namespace manager node contexts, as MSXML
 does.

pushNodeContext() was a stub.  Office resolves the prefixes in a Print
Schema document with it: a feature's name is a QName such as
psk:JobDuplexAllDocumentsContiguously, and MSO pushes the element's
context and asks getURI() what psk means, so with the stub Word never
saw the duplex feature a printer offers.

Measured against MSXML 6 on Windows 11: a pushed context holds the
binding the node's own name makes, then its xmlns declarations and, when
deep, the same for each ancestor, nearest first; a name in no namespace
and xmlns="" leave the prefix unbound.  getURI() with a node looks at
explicit declarations only; lookups go down the whole stack of contexts;
the bottom context only ever holds "xml", so declaring on it opens a new
one; getPrefix()'s index picks among the prefixes bound to a URI;
reset() works; and a buffer has to leave room for the terminator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

